<title>USA: Physiometrix NeuroLink II product cleared.</title>
<headline>Physiometrix NeuroLink II product cleared.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH BILLERICA, Mass. 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Physiometrix Inc said on Wednesday that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has cleared for marketing its NeuroLink II product, a data acquisition system that converts analog brain wave data into digital signals.</p>
<p>The medical products manufacturer said the product can interface with either a personal computer or any EEG machine for data analysis.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that the NeuroLink II builds upon our innovative neuromonitoring technology and expands our market segments,&quot; said company president John Williams.</p>
</text>
